{"questions":[{"question_id":"1GNtj5Ie9AqBBXDS","paperTitle":"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 1 Offline","year":2013,"examDate":2013,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"basics-of-organic-chemistry","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","topic":"electron-displacement-effect","type":"mcqm","marks":2,"negMarks":0.5,"permalink":"the-hyperconjugative-stabilities-of-tert-butyl-cation-and-2-2013-marks-2-1gntj5ie9aqbbxds.htm","content":"The hyperconjugative stabilities of tert-butyl cation and 2-butene, respectively, are due to","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"$$\\sigma \\to p$$ (empty) and $$\\sigma \\to \\pi^*$$ electron delocalisations"},{"identifier":"B","content":"$$\\sigma \\to \\sigma^*$$ and $$\\sigma \\to \\pi$$ electron delocalisations"},{"identifier":"C","content":"$$\\sigma \\to p$$ (filled) and $$\\sigma \\to \\pi$$ electron delocalisations"},{"identifier":"D","content":"p (filled) $$\\to \\sigma^*$$ and $$\\sigma \\to \\pi^*$$ electron delocalisations"}],"correct_options":["A"],"explanation":"<p>(i) The structure of tert-butyl cation $\\left[\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_3\\right)_3 \\mathrm{C}^{\\oplus}\\right]$ is as follows :</p>\n\n<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1lyinhkue/4ea4795f-8492-4112-980a-070548869412/ef5d1d00-4046-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinhkup.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1lyinhkue/4ea4795f-8492-4112-980a-070548869412/ef5d1d00-4046-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinhkup.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 46 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1lyinhkue/4ea4795f-8492-4112-980a-070548869412/ef5d1d00-4046-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinhkup.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1lyinhkue/4ea4795f-8492-4112-980a-070548869412/ef5d1d00-4046-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinhkup.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1lyinhkue/4ea4795f-8492-4112-980a-070548869412/ef5d1d00-4046-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinhkup.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1lyinhkue/4ea4795f-8492-4112-980a-070548869412/ef5d1d00-4046-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinhkup.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1lyinhkue/4ea4795f-8492-4112-980a-070548869412/ef5d1d00-4046-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinhkup.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1lyinhkue/4ea4795f-8492-4112-980a-070548869412/ef5d1d00-4046-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinhkup.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n<p>The carbocation is highly stable due to positive hyperconjugative $(+\\mathrm{H})$ and inductive $(+\\mathrm{I})$ effect.</p>\n\n<p>(ii) The hyperconjugative effect is due to delocalication of $\\sigma$ (sigma) electrons of $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{H}$ sigma ( $\\sigma$ ) bond on carbon adjacent to carbocation with an empty P orbital (on carbcation).</p>\n\n<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1lyinjpfo/7227d8fd-0e25-4015-8025-0af8dc49fd87/2a85eb50-4047-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinjpfp.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1lyinjpfo/7227d8fd-0e25-4015-8025-0af8dc49fd87/2a85eb50-4047-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinjpfp.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 46 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1lyinjpfo/7227d8fd-0e25-4015-8025-0af8dc49fd87/2a85eb50-4047-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinjpfp.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1lyinjpfo/7227d8fd-0e25-4015-8025-0af8dc49fd87/2a85eb50-4047-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinjpfp.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1lyinjpfo/7227d8fd-0e25-4015-8025-0af8dc49fd87/2a85eb50-4047-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinjpfp.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1lyinjpfo/7227d8fd-0e25-4015-8025-0af8dc49fd87/2a85eb50-4047-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinjpfp.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1lyinjpfo/7227d8fd-0e25-4015-8025-0af8dc49fd87/2a85eb50-4047-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinjpfp.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1lyinjpfo/7227d8fd-0e25-4015-8025-0af8dc49fd87/2a85eb50-4047-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinjpfp.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n<p>Hence, carbocation is stabilised due to formation of pi bond with adjacent carbon (due to delocalised) electrons of $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{H}$ sigma bond). Its a s to p (empty) delocalisation.</p>\n\n<p>(iii) There are eight more protons on carbons\nadjacent to carbocation. This gives eight more\nhyperconjugative structures. This impart\nstability to carbocation.</p>\n\n<p>(iv) The structure of 2-butene is as follows :\n<br><br>$$\n\\mathrm{CH}_3-\\mathrm{C}=\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{CH}_3\n$$</p>\n\n<p>The hyperconjugative effect is due to the delocalisation of sigma ( $\\sigma$ ) electrons of $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{H}$ bond with adjacent carbon containing pi bond.</p>\n\n<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1lyinpfip/a3b2722a-16e8-4611-a66a-86f8b0d74961/c9b7b410-4047-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinpfiq.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/jaoe38c1lyinpfip/a3b2722a-16e8-4611-a66a-86f8b0d74961/c9b7b410-4047-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinpfiq.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;max-height:40vh;vertical-align:baseline\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2013 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Basics of Organic Chemistry Question 46 English Explanation 3\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/jaoe38c1lyinpfip/a3b2722a-16e8-4611-a66a-86f8b0d74961/c9b7b410-4047-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinpfiq.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/jaoe38c1lyinpfip/a3b2722a-16e8-4611-a66a-86f8b0d74961/c9b7b410-4047-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinpfiq.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/jaoe38c1lyinpfip/a3b2722a-16e8-4611-a66a-86f8b0d74961/c9b7b410-4047-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinpfiq.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/jaoe38c1lyinpfip/a3b2722a-16e8-4611-a66a-86f8b0d74961/c9b7b410-4047-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinpfiq.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/jaoe38c1lyinpfip/a3b2722a-16e8-4611-a66a-86f8b0d74961/c9b7b410-4047-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinpfiq.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/jaoe38c1lyinpfip/a3b2722a-16e8-4611-a66a-86f8b0d74961/c9b7b410-4047-11ef-a6a6-63cbb58d1d99/file-jaoe38c1lyinpfiq.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n<p>The electrons of $\\mathrm{C}-\\mathrm{H} $ $\\sigma$ bond are donated to anti-bonding $\\left(\\pi^*\\right)$ orbitals of carbon-carbon double bond. Its $\\sigma $ $\\mathrm{s}$ to $\\pi^*$ delocalisation.</p>\n<p>There are five more hydrogens from methyl groups attached to carbon-carbon double bond. Hence, five more hyperconjugative structures.</p>"}]}